e cols | 21 → 36 |\n| 331-360 | `ridge_width` | 0.22 → 0.40 |\n\nFor this short, `Component_Roof` has to be displayed instead of `merge_all`.\n\n**Short 3 (full church, six 60-frame slots):**\n1. **Porch:** Church `step_height` 0.211 → 0.28. Keep step count × step height at 1.8 or less, or the landing slices WindowB.\n2. **Windows:** WindowA height 0.9 → 1.15. For WindowB, height 0.95 → 1.10 while Church `winB_sill_y` goes 2.15 → 1.85, so its top stays put.\n3. **Shutters:** 180 → 0 → 180.\n4. **Shingles:** same two roof parms as short 2.\n5. **\"Facade windows\":** I read this as WindowB `louver_angle` 25 → 55, plus optionally `winA_spacing` 1.6 → 1.3. If you meant the facade itself, Church `plank_count` 28 → 40 also works.\n6. **Roof:** both Church gable heights together, 2.4 → 3.2, upward only.\n\n**Risks:**\n- **Master parms that do nothing:** eight window parms on `/obj/Church` (`winA_width`, `winA_height`, `winA_shutter_angle`, `winA_enable_shutters`, `winB_width`, `winB_height`, `winB_louver_angle`, `winB_louver_count`) are not referenced by anything, so keying them has no visible effect.\n- **Existing keys that would fight the plan:**\n  - WindowA: `shutter_angle` (10 keys over 1-360) and `sash_open_amount` (1-120).\n  - WindowB: `louver_angle` (9 keys) and `center_mullion_width` (5 keys).\n  - The camera rig's `ry` changed between my two reads (the last key moved from frame 240 to 360), so another agent is editing live. Re-read before keying.\n- **The roof follows only the rear gable height:** animating one gable alone opens a gap at the front or makes the facade poke through the roof.\n- **WindowB already hits the timber frame:** the king-post pendant bottom is at y 3.132, but WindowB's top is at 3.315, so the pendant is buried about 0.18 m inside the lintel. Raising WindowB, or lowering either gable, makes this worse.\n- **Wall height breaks the windows:** window heights are absolute, not tied to `wall_height`. Lowering `wall_height` pushes WindowA throug