{"parentUuid":"13d6262a-57cd-4ed1-b4ba-3ff5265fab06","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"39721f1f-e28a-4159-ba71-b4ddfa2c02ea","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1\n# Procedural Church : Hero Asset Coordination, Windows and Roof\n\nDate : 2026-09-11\nAuteur : ZenRay (@zenray.st)\nSujet : Houdini Procedural Church / Hero Asset Coordination (Windows Type A & B, Roof)\nFormat media : 3 Shorts / Reels Master Retina (3456x2234 a 60 fps) + Format 9:16 vertical 4K\n\n---\n\n## Texte du post (Style Damien Richard 3D Tech Artist)\n\n### English Version (Source principale)\n\nHere is the result on my procedural modeling church, still not completely finished but a lot of improvements have been done especially on the hero asset coordination of all parameters.\n\nNew Window Type A and B and the Roof (so hard to make).\n\nIt's already UV-ready, next step will be correct scaling for every component and then texturing phase.\n\nDon't hesitate to follow, more to come / share your thoughts.\n\nFor several weeks, I've been working on the procedural modeling of a bayou church in Houdini for Unreal Engine rendering. A question that seems simple on the surface, but only on the surface, because my goal was to create a successful, parameter-driven hero asset.\n\nTo build this asset and its design, I first designed three separate modules:\n* The cedar shake roof and cresting ridge (Component_Roof)\n* The Gothic shuttered window with muntins (Component_WindowA)\n* The gable pointed arch window with cross (Component_WindowB)\n\nHere is the honest takeaway though: by wanting to break down my church into 3 completely independent HDA components, I made an asset design mistake. It was appealing on paper, but in practice it is counter-productive: when I want to change the roof pitch or global scale, the windows and the roof framing are not linked. I had to manually copy every dimension by hand, otherwise openings end up misaligned or floating in thin air.\n\nThree solid procedural components in their own corner do not make a functional hero asset until they share a common brain. Now that this coordination is done, everything connects properly!\n\nThanks for taking the time to watch and read ᕙ(`▿´)ᕗ\n\n---\n\n### Version Francaise\n\nVoici le resultat sur la modelisation procedurale de ma chapelle bayou, ce n'est pas encore totalement termine mais beaucoup d'ameliorations ont ete apportees, en particulier sur la coordination de tous les parametres au sein du hero asset.\n\nNouvelles Fenetres Type A et B ainsi que la Toiture (tellement difficile a faire).\n\nC'est deja UV-ready, prochaine etape : ajuster le scaling de chaque composant, puis phase de texturing.\n\nN'hesitez pas a vous abonner pour la suite et a partager vos retours.\n\nPendant plusieurs semaines, j'ai bosse sur la modelisation procedurale d'une chapelle bayou sous Houdini pour un rendu sur Unreal Engine. Une question qui parait simple en apparence, mais seulement en apparence, car mon but etait de creer un hero asset reussi et parametrable.\n\nPour construire cet asset et son design, j'avais d'abord concu trois briques separees :\n* La toiture en bardeaux de cedre et faitage (Component_Roof)\n* La fenetre gothique avec volets et croisillons (Component_WindowA)\n* La fenetre pignon a arc brise et croix (Component_WindowB)\n\nMais voila le constat lucide : en voulant decouper mon eglise en 3 composants HDA completement independants, j'avais fait une erreur de design d'asset. C'etait seduisant sur le papier, mais en pratique c'est contre-productif : quand je veux modifier la pente du toit ou l'echelle d'une baie, les fenetres et la charpente ne sont pas liees. Je devais reporter chaque cote a la main sous peine de voir des ouvertures flotter ou briser l'alignement de la facade.\n\nTrois composants proceduraux solides dans leur coin ne font pas un hero asset fonctionnel tant qu'ils ne partagent pas un cerveau commun. Maintenant que cette coordination est en place, tout s'emboite enfin proprement.\n\nMerci d'avoir pris le temps de regarder et de lire ᕙ(`▿´)ᕗ\n\n---\n\n## Decoupage mot a mot des 8 repliques (Sous-titres 15 secondes)\nCalque mot a mot sur le texte anglais ci-dessus :\n\n1. [0.0s a 1.0s] (1.0s) :\n   - L1 (Jaune) : Procedural modeling of a bayou church,\n   - L2 (Blanc) : Hero asset parameter coordination.\n2. [1.0s a 3.0s] (2.0s) :\n   - L1 (Jaune) : New Window Type A, B and Roof,\n   - L2 (Blanc) : So hard to make.\n3. [3.0s a 5.0s] (2.0s) :\n   - L1 (Jaune) : I first designed three separate modules,\n   - L2 (Blanc) : But made an asset design mistake.\n4. [5.0s a 7.0s] (2.0s) :\n   - L1 (Jaune) : 3 independent HDA components\n   - L2 (Blanc) : Was counter-productive in practice.\n5. [7.0s a 9.0s] (2.0s) :\n   - L1 (Jaune) : Now sharing a common brain,\n   - L2 (Blanc) : Everything connects properly.\n6. [9.0s a 11.0s] (2.0s) :\n   - L1 (Jaune) : Geometry is already UV-ready,\n   - L2 (Blanc) : Next step is scaling every component.\n7. [11.0s a 13.0s] (2.0s) :\n   - L1 (Jaune) : Texturing phase coming next,\n   - L2 (Blanc) : For Unreal Engine rendering.\n8. [13.0s a 15.0s] (2.0s) :\n   - L1 (Jaune) : Don't hesitate to follow,\n   - L2 (Blanc) : More to come, share your thoughts!\n(eval):1: ===== not found","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GgxZQEZJVKuHHTE1LVPxnz"}]},"uuid":"ef2de97a-7062-442d-999d-808450c9523c","timestamp":"2026-09-11T20:56:44.626Z","toolUseResult":"Error: Exit code 1\n# Procedural Church : Hero Asset Coordination, Windows and Roof\n\nDate : 2026-09-11\nAuteur : ZenRay (@zenray.st)\nSujet : Houdini Procedural Church / Hero Asset Coordination (Windows Type A & B, Roof)\nFormat media : 3 Shorts / Reels Master Retina (3456x2234 a 60 fps) + Format 9:16 vertical 4K\n\n---\n\n## Texte du post (Style Damien Richard 3D Tech Artist)\n\n### English Version (Source principale)\n\nHere is the result on my procedural modeling church, still not completely finished but a lot of impro